   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Behind the wheel",
     "texto": [
      "Useful verbs: **conducir**, **adelantar**, **frenar**, **girar** and **aparcar**. **Abrocharse el cinturón** is fastening your seat belt; **llevar el carné de conducir** is carrying your driving licence.\n\nOn the road there are **carriles**, **semáforos** and **pasos de cebra** for **peatones**. The general maximum speed for cars on a motorway is 120 km/h, unless a sign shows a lower one.\n\nThere may be **atascos**; **multas** can be given for speeding or bad parking; a tyre can get a puncture (**pincharse**) and a car can run out of petrol. If it breaks down, call **la grúa** or **el seguro** and take it to **el taller**.\n\nRules use impersonal forms: **no se puede adelantar**; **está prohibido aparcar**; **hay que ceder el paso a los peatones**; **es obligatorio abrocharse el cinturón**. And for what happens by accident: **se me pinchó una rueda**, **se nos acabó la gasolina**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Rules, accidents and «se me»",
     "texto": [
      "There are three very common resources on the road:\n\n- **General rules**: **es obligatorio**, **está prohibido**, **no se puede** or **hay que** + infinitive. **Es obligatorio abrocharse el cinturón.**\n- **What happens by accident**: **se** + **me / te / le / nos / os / les** + verb. The verb agrees with what breaks or runs out. **Se nos pinchó una rueda.**\n- **Someone you do not name**: the third person plural. **Me pusieron una multa.**"
     ],
